n Police's tech team leads  them back to a different house where  Rigg hits pause in the VCR to determine  that the game that they had been  watching on the screens all along was  already over one question you might have  had is where jigsaw is getting all of  these empty houses and buildings fans of  the franchise know that John Kramer was  once involved in a project called the  urban renewal group which helps provide  housing to low-income families but he  abandoned the endeavor halfway through I  think if the nerve gas house was going  to be one of these homes but John  reinforced it to make it the setting of  his game the fake-out house was probably  a replica or model home which would  explain why it has the same layout and  why jigsaw was able to trick the SWAT  team the twist in this movie works great  because as the audience were on the same  level as the protagonist the police we  are being presented the events out of  order because that's how they are  perceiving the situation we find out the  truth as they find out whereas in a  movie like jigsaw the story is told the  way that it is just to trick the  audience there's no other practical  reason for doing it that way and it  feels artificial another thing that saw  two gets right that you may not have  thought about is the theming of the  traps to fit the character who is  playing them for example it seems the  needle pit room was once a nursery you  see a  he's written on the walls baby bottles  toys carriages and even creepy little  infant mannequins Xavier has revealed to  have been a drug dealer who took  advantage of his clients addictions when  a junkie becomes addicted their body  becomes dependent on the drugs just as a  baby in a nursery needs its parents to  provide for its the drug addicts need to  keep crawling back to Xavier to get  their fix  desperation seems to be a key theme in  the film had Abby not been so desperate  to get both antidotes he could have seen  the nozzle to turn off the f